# Discarding to hand size at cleanup is discarding (CR 514.1, 701.9a), so Marauding Mako grows: Bot1 casts it on turn 1 and
# then plays no more lands, so its hand grows by a card each turn from five to eight on turn 7, and the one card it must
# discard puts a +1/+1 counter on the Mako. Before then, at seven cards, it discards nothing and the Mako stays a 1/1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Marauding Mako
Mountain x5
Mountain x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Marauding Mako.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.End]
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 7
? Bot1.Battlefield.Marauding Mako.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
[T7 Bot1.Cleanup]
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 8
[T9 Bot1.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Turn = 9
Bot1.Battlefield.Marauding Mako.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Marauding Mako.Power = 2
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 1
